description:
Refactor Task-3 (comments UI) to use the new backend deep merge capability.

## Background
Backend v0.2.18 now does deep merge on properties, so we no longer need to fetch the full node before updating.

## Old Approach (Workaround)
```javascript
// Had to fetch full node to avoid losing other properties
const node = await getNode(label);
const properties = { ...node.properties };
properties.comments = [...(properties.comments || []), newComment];
await updateNode(label, { properties });
```

## New Approach (Simplified)
```javascript
// Can now send just the comments array
const comments = [...existingComments, newComment];
await updateNode(label, { 
    properties: { comments } 
});
// Other properties (severity, component, etc.) are preserved!
```

## Benefits
- Simpler code
- Fewer API calls (no need to GET before PATCH)
- Less risk of race conditions
- Works with nested property updates too

## Implementation Notes
- Still need to track existing comments for the UI list
- Deep merge replaces arrays, doesn't append to them
- So we still need to include full comments array, just not other properties
